# policy_psweep run matrix  (read by scripts/launch.sh)
#
# Sweeps the victim predictability p (prob its best action is correct) across and
# around the reward EV-flip band (0.143, 0.353). MULTIPLE victim lines: each is
# crossed with every neighbor and config. Output .out files are named
# <victim>_<neighbor>_<config>.out (consumed by rollup.py).
#
#   victim   <name> <source> [prog-args...]
#   neighbor <name> <source> [prog-args...]
#   config   <name> <ini>
#
# The victim prog-arg is p in PER-MILLE (p*1000); the name encodes it (vp250 =>
# p=0.250). 5 values inside the band, 4 outside (2 below 0.143, 2 above 0.353).

# --- below the band (p < 0.143): abstain-leaning even without the attack ---
victim vp010  victim.c  10
victim vp030  victim.c  30
victim vp050  victim.c  50
victim vp100  victim.c  100
# --- inside the EV-flip band (0.143 < p < 0.353): CONTESTABLE ---
victim vp160  victim.c  160
victim vp200  victim.c  200
victim vp250  victim.c  250
victim vp300  victim.c  300
victim vp340  victim.c  340
# --- above the band (p > 0.353): gamble wins even under HBW reward (resists) ---
victim vp450  victim.c  450
victim vp800  victim.c  800

# attacker intensities -> the bw3 levels on the y-axis grouping
neighbor atk_idle    attacker.c  idle
neighbor atk_light   attacker.c  light
neighbor atk_medium  attacker.c  medium
neighbor atk_heavy   attacker.c  heavy

# reward table LIVE (the attack). Degree pinned equal => action-selection only.
config   aware   aware.ini
